  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Ceftaroline fosamil is a cephalosporin antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections such as community-acquired pneumonia, skin infections, and staphylococcal infections. It is approved and authorised in the European Union, where it is used for these infections.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q409712&quot;>Wikidata Q409712</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>ceftaroline fosamil</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>J01DI02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB06590&quot;>DB06590</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/9852981&quot;>9852981</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:70718&quot;>70718</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q409712&quot;>Q409712</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C22H21N8O8PS4</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>684.672 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
